use ./lib

export test InitCommand:
    expects:
        Piton should have an init command that provides a quick way to set up a
        new project with a piton.config.pi file with a handful of presets.

export test InitAsAPlugin:
    expects:
        The init command should be implemented as a plugin, and the templates
        should be easily editable and extensible by the Piton authors.

export test Templates:
    expects:
        The init command templates should be store in templates/ directory of
        the plugin.

export test ProjectTypes:
    expects:
        `piton init` asks for the project's name first, unless it is given as
        `piton init name`, and uses it as both the name and the directory, so
        `.` takes the current directory's name. It then asks which type of
        project to start: basic, application or tether. A basic project picks
        what it compiles to: JSON, Markdown or YAML. An application chooses
        whether it uses Belay, and with Belay which agents it supports and its
        codeRoot and shapeRoot, with sane defaults, and whether it adds testing.
        A tether can't use Belay, though it shows with an example skill that a
        package can ship agent guidance, and can add testing configured against
        the specification only. Testing is added unless declined. Last comes the
        option to add the crux skills.
